# Gapless fast path, part 2 of 6: the loader gate cave (first 32 bytes;
# 0025 holds its last instruction).
name: gapless-2-gate-cave
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051664
gate: build refuses unless the 32 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: The gate, entered from the hook at 0x0306cb2c (0021) with
  r0 = decoder module id. It reuses the resident decoder only when both
  hold: (1) core 1 is running, read from the stock flag at 0x03004138
  (address in the 0023 literal), which the halt routine 0x0306cb0c
  clears and the core-1 boot handshake sets; (2) the retained module
  word at 0x030515b0 (0020), masked to 7 bits, equals the requested
  module. Then it branches to the warm-start extension (0034), which
  stores module|0x80, sets the monitor's start-of-track counter, and
  returns to the codec case,
  skipping the image re-copy, the core-1 reset, the parameter-page copy
  and the ready poll; the 0x65 open exchange and the rest of load-start
  run as stock. Otherwise it records the module, re-executes the two
  displaced instructions (push {r4,r5,r6,lr}; mov r5, r0) and branches
  to the stock body at 0x0306cb30 (0025). Condition (1) is what v1
  lacked: the stock stop path halts core 1 (reset 0x32 held, clock 2
  gated) on every track change, so a module match alone skipped the
  reboot of a halted core. The transition rig
  (patches/gapless/rig/) shows v1 timing out the open exchange (5.5 s)
  and starting I2S on an unrefilled buffer. As built here the module
  compare is followed by an unconditional branch to the stock path;
  0026 turns it into `bne`. The cave occupies 16 `bx lr` stub slots at
  0x03051664..0x03051683 in the module-0 stub farm: the exhaustive
  reference scan (BL/B.W targets, literal words, MOVW/MOVT pairs, all
  82 modules) shows zero references to the range, and the function
  before it ends in `pop {r4,r5,r6,pc}` at 0x03051662, so nothing falls
  through into it. Bytes: patches/gapless/tools/assemble_v2.py.
expect: 7047704770477047704770477047704770477047704770477047704770477047
